review_comments:
The thing with debouncing these `Flash()` / `Miss()` calls that worries me is the `JudgementResult` parameter. Debouncing these with `AddOnce()` means that if more than one judgement result incurs a flash / miss in a single frame, implementors of `HealthDisplay` will only see the second result.

The funny thing is that _none_ of the existing implementations of `Flash()` / `Miss()` use the judgement result for _anything_. But the point to me is moreso that this API design creates the _expectation_ that a health display will have `Flash()` called for every successful result (that isn't an `IgnoreHit`, I guess), and `Miss()` called for every miss, and try to do things around that, and utterly fail because the debounce will potentially silently eat some of the calls.

I guess my point here is for added safety I'd be for removing the `JudgementResult` param from here and all overrides and related methods. Something along the lines of:

